    "sbar": {
      "situation": "The bank payment system has recovered. Two recovery checks in a row, the last at 24 s, ran the main journey cleanly.",
      "background": "The screening primary began timing out, with p95 at 1818 ms against a 14 ms baseline. Calls to screening failed 100%, so 96% of requests failed and the payments step returned 503. Separately, the clearing worker was terminated (exit code 15) and stopped answering, leaving 17 items in its queue.",
      "assessment": "Root cause one was a slow screening dependency (confidence 0.9); the incident commander itself failed screening over to screening-standby, which now serves it. Root cause two was the clearing process being down (confidence 0.85); item 90 had 0 attempts, so no item was crashing it, and the incident commander itself restarted clearing, which is back up. Gateway and payments had no changes and failed only because of screening.",
      "recommendation": "Investigate why the screening primary slowed before failing back from standby, and find what sent exit code 15 to the clearing worker. Operations should confirm the 17-item clearing backlog, starting at item 90, drains fully. They should also review payments rejected with 503 during the outage for customer or money impact."
    },
